IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `re42-nouns`
IMPORT `re42-published-figures`
IMPORT `re42-s47-appreciation`
IMPORT `re42-s49-exemptions`
IMPORT `re42-s48a-rates`

-- Row il-42. TESTS OF THE SELLER'S SEAT: section 47 (the appreciation), sections 49 to 49F (the exemptions), section 48A (the rates).
-- The inputs and the reading of the text are set by hand; the arithmetic of the expected values (day counts, products, sums) was computed in Python, an instrument independent of this encoding, and the comment above each assertion shows it.
-- The two Ordinance rates in the rate tests (47% and 50%, or 20%) are STIPULATED for the tests: they are not published figures and no part of the encoding holds them.
-- The sale prices are round numbers chosen to land on the edges of the ceilings; none is a market figure.

-- BUILDERS. Each fills every fact of A sale of a dwelling; the facts a family does not vary take a default that makes no exemption available (asked: FALSE; served as a dwelling: 0 of 100 months).

GIVETH A LIST OF `An expense you paid`
`no expenses` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A LIST OF `A dwelling that may stand against the seller`
`no other dwellings` MEANS EMPTY

GIVEN holder IS A `Who holds a dwelling`
      share IS A NUMBER
      assoc IS A BOOLEAN
      inherited IS A BOOLEAN
      protected IS A BOOLEAN
      inIsrael IS A BOOLEAN
      replacement IS A MAYBE DATE
      inheritedOk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A dwelling that may stand against the seller`
`a dwelling` MEANS
    `A dwelling that may stand against the seller` WITH
        `held by` IS holder
        `the share of it that you and those treated as one seller with you hold together, as a fraction of the whole` IS share
        `it is owned through an association, and is not the association's stock in trade` IS assoc
        `it came to the holder by inheritance` IS inherited
        `it was let under a protected tenancy before 1 January 1997` IS protected
        `it lies in Israel or in the Area` IS inIsrael
        `the day you bought it, if you bought it as a replacement for the dwelling sold` IS replacement
        `it was inherited from someone who owned only one dwelling, and you are their spouse, a descendant, or the spouse of a descendant` IS inheritedOk

GIVETH A LIST OF `A dwelling that may stand against the seller`
`one dwelling standing against you` MEANS
    LIST (`a dwelling` `you` 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE)

GIVEN kind IS A `The kind of an expense you paid`
      amount IS A NUMBER
      divisor IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `An expense you paid`
`an expense of the kind` MEANS
    `An expense you paid` WITH
        `its kind` IS kind
        `its amount` IS amount
        `the index the Law divides by for that kind` IS divisor

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two numbers agree to a cent` MEANS (x MINUS y) LESS THAN 0.01 AND (y MINUS x) LESS THAN 0.01

GIVEN x IS A MAYBE NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the answer is the number` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN JUST p THEN `the two numbers agree to a cent` p y
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN x IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the answer is missing` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN JUST p THEN FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

`the rates stipulated for the tests` MEANS
    `The Ordinance rates you state` WITH
        `the rate at which section 121 of the Ordinance would tax the appreciation as the top step of your income` IS 0.47
        `the highest rate in section 121 of the Ordinance` IS 0.5

`the rates stipulated for the tests, top step at 20 percent` MEANS
    `The Ordinance rates you state` WITH
        `the rate at which section 121 of the Ordinance would tax the appreciation as the top step of your income` IS 0.2
        `the highest rate in section 121 of the Ordinance` IS 0.5


-- Readers of the parts, so that an assertion is one line.
GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the part: up to the start day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parts of the real appreciation` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `up to the start day`)

GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the part: after the start day up to the change day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parts of the real appreciation` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `after the start day up to the change day`)

GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the part: after the change day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parts of the real appreciation` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `after the change day`)

GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the part: up to the transition day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parts of the real appreciation by the transition day` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `up to the transition day`)

GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the part: after the transition day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parts of the real appreciation by the transition day` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `after the transition day`)


GIVEN saleDay IS A DATE
      acqDay IS A DATE
      consideration IS A NUMBER
      acqValue IS A NUMBER
      expenses IS A LIST OF `An expense you paid`
      depreciation IS A NUMBER
      idxSale IS A NUMBER
      idxAcq IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A sale of a dwelling`
`a sale for appreciation` MEANS
    `A sale of a dwelling` WITH
        `the day of the sale` IS saleDay
        `the day you acquired the right` IS acqDay
        `the consideration you received` IS consideration
        `the value of the right on the day you acquired it` IS acqValue
        `the expenses you paid` IS expenses
        `the depreciation allowed` IS depreciation
        `the index on the day of the sale` IS idxSale
        `the index on the day you acquired the right` IS idxAcq
        `you are an Israeli resident` IS TRUE
        `you are a non-resident with no dwelling in the country where you are resident` IS FALSE
        `you sold all your rights in the dwelling` IS TRUE
        `the months in the period for which the appreciation is computed, not counting any time before 1 January 1998` IS 100
        `the months in that period that the dwelling served mainly as a dwelling, counting months of no use and months of education or religion` IS 0
        `the dwelling served mainly as a dwelling through all four years before the sale` IS FALSE
        `your other dwellings at the sale` IS `no other dwellings`
        `the months you have been the owner since it became a dwelling` IS 24
        `the number of months back from this sale in which you sold another dwelling free of tax under the only-dwelling exemption` IS NOTHING
        `you received the dwelling by inheritance` IS FALSE
        `you are the spouse or a descendant of the deceased, or the spouse of a descendant` IS FALSE
        `the deceased owned only one dwelling when they died` IS FALSE
        `the deceased would have been exempt had they sold it` IS FALSE
        `you asked for the exemption when you filed the declaration under section 73` IS FALSE
        `you received the dwelling as a gift` IS FALSE
        `you received at least half the price of the dwelling as a gift in the three years before you bought it` IS FALSE
        `the months since you became the owner of the dwelling, counted from your 18th birthday if you were under 18 when you became the owner` IS 100
        `the months since you began to live in the dwelling as its owner, counted from your 18th birthday if you were under 18 then; nothing if it was never your regular home` IS NOTHING
        `what you sold is a share of a dwelling within the limit of section 49C(3), or a dwelling let under a protected tenancy before 1 January 1997` IS FALSE
        `that share or dwelling was disregarded under section 49C when you sold another dwelling free of tax under the only-dwelling exemption` IS FALSE
        `you hold exactly one other dwelling` IS FALSE
        `you sold that other dwelling free of tax within 12 months after this sale` IS FALSE
        `the value of the one other dwelling you hold, if you hold exactly one` IS 0
        `the combined value of the sold dwelling and the one other dwelling you hold` IS 0
        `you bought another dwelling in the year before the sale of the other dwelling or will buy one in the year after, for at least three quarters of the combined value` IS FALSE
        `you have used the one-off exemption before` IS FALSE

