-- Neither fact: ordinary.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a protected-share sale` FALSE FALSE)) 3_000_000
-- A small share, but the presumption was not used before: allowed.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a protected-share sale` TRUE FALSE)) 3_000_000
-- A small share whose presumption was used for an earlier exempt sale: the paragraph does not apply.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a protected-share sale` TRUE TRUE)) 0
-- THE ONE-OFF EXEMPTION, s 49E. `a one-off sale day consideration oneOther sold12 otherValue combined boughtAlt usedBefore`; the other dwelling stands against you, so only s 49E can exempt.
-- Combined value exactly 2,252,000: s 49E(a), all of the sale value.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 1 3 2025) 1_500_000 TRUE TRUE 700_000 2_252_000 TRUE FALSE)) 1_500_000
-- Combined 2,252,001, other dwelling 700,000: s 49E(a1) exempts min(1,552,001; 2,252,000 - 700,000 = 1,552,000).
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 1 3 2025) 1_552_001 TRUE TRUE 700_000 2_252_001 TRUE FALSE)) 1_552_000
-- Combined exactly 3,746,000, other dwelling 1,000,000: exempt min(2,746,000; 2,252,000 - 1,000,000 = 1,252,000).
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 1 3 2025) 2_746_000 TRUE TRUE 1_000_000 3_746_000 TRUE FALSE)) 1_252_000
-- Combined one shekel above 3,746,000: no exemption.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 1 3 2025) 2_746_001 TRUE TRUE 1_000_000 3_746_001 TRUE FALSE)) 0
-- Used before: s 49E(b).
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 1 3 2025) 1_500_000 TRUE TRUE 700_000 2_252_000 TRUE TRUE)) 0
-- No alternative dwelling bought: s 49E(a)(4).
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 1 3 2025) 1_500_000 TRUE TRUE 700_000 2_252_000 FALSE FALSE)) 0
-- The other dwelling not sold within 12 months: s 49E(a)(2).
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 1 3 2025) 1_500_000 TRUE FALSE 700_000 2_252_000 TRUE FALSE)) 0
-- Not exactly one other dwelling: s 49E(a)(1).
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 1 3 2025) 1_500_000 FALSE TRUE 700_000 2_252_000 TRUE FALSE)) 0
-- 1 January 2028: the amounts of s 49E are not held for that day: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the answer is missing` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 1 1 2028) 1_500_000 TRUE TRUE 700_000 2_252_000 TRUE FALSE))
-- 31 December 2024: the earlier amounts are not held: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the answer is missing` (`the sale value that is exempt` (`a one-off sale` (Date 31 12 2024) 1_500_000 TRUE TRUE 700_000 2_252_000 TRUE FALSE))

§§ `Section 48A: the rates`

-- Every rate sale: 3,000,000 against 2,000,000 acquisition value, indexes equal, so the real appreciation is 1,000,000 and the inflationary amount 0. Ordinance rates stipulated: 47% and 50%.
-- Acquired 2015, not a qualifying dwelling, no exemption: s 48A(b)(1), min(25%, 47%) x 1,000,000 = 250,000; no chargeable inflationary amount for a right acquired after 1993.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) 3_000_000 0 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 250_000
-- The same with the Ordinance's top step at 20%: min(25%, 20%) x 1,000,000 = 200,000.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) 3_000_000 0 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests, top step at 20 percent`) 200_000
-- A qualifying dwelling acquired on or after the transition day: s 48A(b)(1), 250,000 (no exemption asked).
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) 3_000_000 100 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 250_000
-- A qualifying dwelling acquired 1 January 2010, sold 1 January 2026, no exemption asked: s 48A(b2): real appreciation up to the transition day is exempt (1,461 of 5,844 days = a quarter); the balance 750,000 x 25%% = 187,500; the inflationary amount at 0%.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2010) 3_000_000 100 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 187_500
-- A qualifying dwelling acquired 1 January 1993: the inflationary amount is not computed, but at 0%% it needs no computing, so the answer stands: balance after the transition day x 25%%.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 1993) 3_000_000 100 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 90910.97652
-- NOT qualifying, acquired 1 January 2010: s 48A(b1): nothing up to the start day (acquired after it); 124743.3265 of the appreciation between the start day and the change day at min(20%, 47%) = 20%; the rest at 25%.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2010) 3_000_000 0 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 243762.833676
-- NOT qualifying, acquired 1 January 2001: all three parts. Up to the start day (310 of 9,131 days) at the highest rate of s 121 (50%% stipulated); start day to the day before the change day at 20%%; the rest at 25%%.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2001) 3_000_000 0 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 238194.064177
-- NOT qualifying, acquired 1 January 1993: the chargeable inflationary amount needs the index on 31 December 1993, which is not held: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the answer is missing` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 1993) 3_000_000 0 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`)
-- Acquired on 31 December 1960: s 48A(d) is not encoded: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the answer is missing` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 1960) 3_000_000 0 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`)
-- A sale on 31 May 2023, before the day the present wording is taken to govern: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the answer is missing` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 31 5 2023) (Date 1 1 2015) 3_000_000 0 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`)
-- A sale on 1 June 2023: the first day the wording is taken to govern (assumed, not read).
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 6 2023) (Date 1 1 2015) 3_000_000 0 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 250_000
-- A qualifying dwelling, exemption asked, only dwelling, 3,000,000 under the ceiling: no tax.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) 3_000_000 100 TRUE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 0
-- Sold for 6,000,000 (real appreciation 4,000,000): exempt up to the 5,008,000 ceiling; the taxable fraction 992,000/6,000,000 carries a quarter of 4,000,000.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2015) 6_000_000 100 TRUE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 165333.333333
-- The same exemption claimed on 1 January 2028: the ceiling for that day is not held: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the answer is missing` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 1 2028) (Date 1 1 2015) 3_000_000 100 TRUE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`)
-- No exemption asked on 1 January 2028: no ceiling needed, the tax is 250,000.
#ASSERT `the answer is the number` (`the appreciation tax on your sale` (`a sale for the rates` (Date 1 1 2028) (Date 1 1 2015) 3_000_000 0 FALSE) `the rates stipulated for the tests`) 250_000
#ASSERT `where the rates of section 48A were read` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
